<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="set-bonuses">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_treasurechest02b.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tier &amp; Set Bonuses for Blood Death Knight in Mists of Pandaria Classic</span></h2>The Blood Death Knight has one of the strongest 2-set bonuses, bringing uptime of <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=49222/bone-shield">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_deathknight_boneshield.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bone Shield</span></a> from approximately 50% while permanently tanking to roughly 80%. In a fight where there are periods of downtime where the DK is not actively tanking, that uptime becomes closer to 100%. <br/>
<br/>One of the biggest reasons why Blood Death Knights are more prone to dying than other tanks is that they lack reliable, consistent active mitigation, meaning they can quite frequently take completely unmitigated attacks. The 2-set bonus essentially fixes this issue. <br/>
<br/>The 4-set bonus is rather lackluster, but may have fantastic utility situationally. Despite being 6 item level lower than the non-tier options, picking up the additional two pieces to attain the 4-set bonus is still worth it, but I'd recommend passing tokens after the initial 2, as other classes will make much better use out of their tier bonuses. <br/>
<br/>Every time the DK uses <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=49028/dancing-rune-weapon">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dancing Rune Weapon</span></a>, they regain all of their runes, acting as an <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=89831/empower-rune-weapon">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_62.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Empower Rune Weapon</span></a>. This means that the DK should aim to be as rune-starved as possible before using Dancing Rune Weapon. <br/>
<br/>
<b>Honorable Mention:</b> The DPS Tier 15 2-set bonus is still the highest DPS option for us as Blood Death Knights due to how the ghoul from the set scales with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=93099/vengeance">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_charm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vengeance</span></a>. The increased throughput is generally not worth the loss in survivability, but can be worth considering if all other offensive trades have been exhausted.<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="tier-16-tank">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">Tank Tier 16 - <a data-entity="item-set" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item-set=1201/plate-of-cyclopean-dread">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Plate of Cyclopean Dread</span></a></span></h3>
<div class="wh-center" style="text-align: -webkit-center;">
