<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>As with the <span class="q5">legendary meta gem</span>, we have access to both an offensive and defensive option when it comes to the legendary cloaks. <br/>
<br/>
<b>Which should you use? </b>Well, the answer is not black and white. As you head into Siege of Orgimmar progression, most people should default to <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102250/qian-ying-fortitude-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_oxtank_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao</span></a>, especially for the later bosses. <br/>
<br/>
<a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102250/qian-ying-fortitude-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_oxtank_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao</span></a> operates as a cheat death with a 2-minute cooldown. It's unique in the way that it functions, however. If you have 90% health, take a massive swing that would've killed you; the cloak will absorb the entire hit, leaving you at 90% health after the cloak procs. On the flip side, if you are tanking many small adds and have 2% health before taking a fatal hit, the cloak will put you back at 2% health, which will likely not save you from dying. If you do happen to die while the effect of the cloak is on cooldown, the cooldown will be cleared when you resurrect.  <br/>
<br/>This cloak should be used when you're expecting to take large hits in fights such as Garrosh Hellscream, Paragons of the Klaxxi, and Iron Juggernaut. <br/>
<br/>
<a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102249/gong-lu-strength-of-xuen">
<img alt="Gong-Lu, Strength of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_tigermelee_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gong-Lu, Strength of Xuen</span></a> procs a continuous frontal cleave approximately two times per minute. This effect scales with Attack Power from <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=93099/vengeance">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_charm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vengeance</span></a> and is responsible for approximately 5% of your overall damage on single target encounters. Where this effect shines is on encounters where cleave damage is valued or where you are very unlikely to make use of the cheat death effect of <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102250/qian-ying-fortitude-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_oxtank_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao</span></a>. <br/>
<br/>This cloak should be used when offensive throughput is valued on multiple targets on fights like <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=71889/secured-stockpile-of-pandaren-spoils">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Secured Stockpile of Pandaren Spoils</span></a> and <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=72249/galakras">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Galakras</span></a>
<div class="box" data-level="null">
<div class="wh-center" style="text-align: -webkit-center;">
<b>
<span class="c6">Special Note for Death Knights</span></b></div>
<br/>Early in the original Mists of Pandaria cycle, the effect of <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102250/qian-ying-fortitude-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_oxtank_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao</span></a> was proccing at the same time as <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=114556/purgatory">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_shadowegg.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Purgatory</span></a>, making it essentially useless. However, on the version of the game we're playing right now, the effect from the cloak will always proc <b>before</b> Purgatory, making you have two separate cheat deaths as a Death Knight.</div>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_03.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Blood Death Knight Trinkets in Phase 5</span></h2>Trinkets become very interesting in SoO, as there are a lot of niche interactions that can completely change rotations and the way you approach a fight. That being said, the philosophy around trinkets and gearing hasn't changed. Trinkets like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105568/vial-of-living-corruption">
<img alt="Vial of Living Corruption" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_10.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vial of Living Corruption</span></a> will give you the most survivability, while trinkets like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105632/skeers-bloodsoaked-talisman">
<img alt="Skeer's Bloodsoaked Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Skeer's Bloodsoaked Talisman</span></a> will give you the most offensive utility. What trinket one should use will depend on the encounter and overall tanking philosophy. <br/>
<br/>Changing trinkets on an encounter-by-encounter basis is encouraged.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>
<ins>Offensive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105632/skeers-bloodsoaked-talisman">
<img alt="Skeer's Bloodsoaked Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Skeer's Bloodsoaked Talisman</span></a> - This is by far your strongest offensive trinket. A skilled Death Knight will try to snapshot their diseases at the tail end of the trinket's proc effect for a nearly 100% crit snapshot. <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=49028/dancing-rune-weapon">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dancing Rune Weapon</span></a> also snapshots crit, meaning in an ideal world you would like to use both Dancing Rune Weapon and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=77575/outbreak">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathvortex.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Outbreak</span></a> for a double disease snapshot.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
